Report the game library's bots in status replies and `rcon status`

Applies to q2pro at commit 601a8df8433b0c50dbbe37c0716c3793fff140a7.
`server/enginepatch.sh` checks that it still does.

Carried rather than upstreamed: it is a change colosseum wants from the engine
it runs on, and a q2pro that does not carry it runs colosseum perfectly well --
the bots just stay invisible to the outside.

WHAT IT FIXES

Gladiator-derived bots -- colosseum's, and every Quake II mod descended from
Mr. Elusive's 1999 game source -- are created entirely inside the GAME. The bot
is handed one of the game's client edicts and its ClientConnect runs, but
nothing ever connects, so the engine holds no client_t for that slot. Both
places the engine reports players from walk `sv_clientlist`, which only
SV_DirectConnect ever appends to, so a server with eight bots playing
advertises itself as empty:

    $ printf '\xff\xff\xff\xffstatus\x00' | nc -u <server> 27910
    ...\maxclients\24...
    0 164 "WallFly[BZZZ]"          <- the only real connection

    $ rcon status
    No UDP clients.

This is not a q2pro regression. id's 1997 server is identical on the point
(SV_StatusString in server/sv_main.c iterates svs.clients and requires
cs_connected/cs_spawned, and SV_DirectConnect is the only way into that state),
and so are yquake2 and q2repro. Quake III solved it the other way round, in the
engine: SV_BotAllocateClient takes a real client_t and marks it NA_BOT, which
is a service Q2's game_import_t has no equivalent of.

WHAT IT DOES

Adds a read-only report of client slots the game has filled that the engine has
no connection for, and includes them in the three places a player list is
produced:

  * SVC_Status  -- the UDP status reply browsers and the master list read
  * SVC_Info    -- the N/M player count, via SV_CountClients
  * SV_Status_f -- the console/rcon listing, WHICH IS THE ONE WALLFLY POLLS
                   (see filter-rcon-status.sh); its LIST_EMPTY early-out had
                   to learn that a bots-only server is not an empty one

A bot row carries the bot's name from the playerskins configstring, its live
frag count from the edict's player state, and a ping of 0.

WHAT IT DOES NOT DO

No client_t is allocated and sv_clientlist is not touched, so none of the 45
FOR_EACH_CLIENT loops in the server change behaviour: the connection path, the
frame builder, the netchan, the timeout check and the anticheat never see
anything new. Consequently the engine still accepts a connection while the
browser shows the server full, and the game still relocates a bot to make room
(colosseum's BotMoveToFreeClientEdict). With colosseum's 18-bot roster against
maxclients 24 that case cannot arise.

It needs NO change to the game library. The detection rides on GMF_PROPERINUSE,
which colosseum advertises unconditionally, and on the playerskins configstring
the game writes for its bots anyway. SVF_BOT is deliberately not used: colosseum
only sets it when protocol extensions are negotiated, and g_protocol_extensions
defaults to 0.

OFF SWITCH

    set sv_status_show_bots 0

reverts every one of the three replies to stock q2pro output, with no restart.
Default is 1.

VERIFIED

Built natively against the pinned commit and run with colosseum's game library,
gladiator.so and four bots on q2dm7 under g_ruleset dm: status listed all four
by name with live scores, `info 34` reported 4/20, and `rcon status` printed
them in slots 16-19 -- the high ones, which is G_SpawnClient searching downward
(R-BOT-14). With sv_status_show_bots 0 the same running server produced stock
replies: empty player list, 0/20, "No UDP clients."

